{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK13ClientProfileO8standardyA2CmF","roleHeading":"Case","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"standard","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ClientProfile.standard","symbolKind":"case"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientProfile"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"standard","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/clientprofile\/standard"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientProfile\/standard","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"Self::Standard":{"identifier":"Self::Standard","title":"Standard","url":"Self::Standard","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Standard"}],"type":"link"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","kind":"symbol","title":"AxiamSDK","abstract":[{"text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management).","type":"text"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/ClientProfile/standard":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientProfile\/standard","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"standard"}],"title":"ClientProfile.standard","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/clientprofile\/standard","kind":"symbol"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/ClientProfile":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientProfile","title":"ClientProfile","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ClientProfile"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/clientprofile","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ClientProfile"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Which security posture a client is registered under (X5.1). This is the FAPI “one switch”.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"FAPI 2.0 is not a single feature but a bundle of constraints — mandatory PAR, mandatory PKCE","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with ","type":"text"},{"code":"S256","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", mandatory strong client authentication, mandatory sender-constrained tokens,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and a refusal of every relaxation the base specs permit. Encoding them as one profile rather","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than a dozen independent booleans means an operator cannot register a client that is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"nearly","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" FAPI, and a reviewer can answer “is this client financial-grade?” by reading one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"field. The same philosophy as the rate-limit postures: ordinary clients see no behaviour","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change at all, because ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"Self::Standard","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is the serde default and every row","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written before schema v38 decodes to it.","type":"text"}]}}}